{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Hypnotic Eye feels like a natural next choice after You Should Be So Lucky because the Tom Petty connection gives me a familiar rock sound I want to keep exploring.",
    "A Fool To Care follows my interest in Memphis through Boz Scaggs's soulful blues, while live Hendrix and Born To Play Guitar also connect with my interest in expressive guitar playing."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shadows in the Night misses what I want now: interpretations of older standards do not offer the blues and guitar-driven rock that draw me in.",
    "Band of Brothers and Django and Jimmie lean toward country when that is not my current interest, and the Sons of Anarchy soundtrack gives me no clear connection to an artist or show I am seeking."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in established musicians seems to have been stretched into an interest in their music regardless of the sound of the particular album.",
    "A broad connection through roots-oriented music is not enough to make country collaborations, tribute albums, and soundtrack collections equally appealing to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The direct connection from You Should Be So Lucky to Tom Petty, and from Memphis to more Boz Scaggs, matters more to me than a loose resemblance between albums.",
    "I choose very little at a time. Live Hendrix, blues guitar, and reflective songwriting can appeal without making me ready to choose them today; familiarity and a clear connection decide my immediate selections."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar blues and rock, but stretched it too far into country, standards, and collections without a strong personal connection."
}"}
